  "selection": "Three strict event laws on the same sixteen states. Horizon 2. Initial state 0. The label is 1 when bit 1 equals bit 2 and 0 otherwise. The subset is the states with label 1. The free law toggles each of the four bits with weight 1. The coupled law toggles bit 0 and bit 3 and jointly flips bits 1 and 2. The frozen-copy law toggles only bit 0 and bit 3. Each named weight is 1. The stored fields are the horizon distribution, the subset probability, and strong lumpability of the label. An inexact partition stores no quotient rows. The clock is one declared event, applied twice. This is not an intervention. The laws are restated in this plan. The question is ATLAS-Q13 and stays open. One partition does not settle a two-stage quotient. No occupation is requested.",
